# Rule 3: a fold is over a bounded range, a count known before the fold
# starts (IsBoundedRange, :chain, #1172).  A standard fold is called only
# inside a function whose range parameter is constrained by IsBoundedRange:
# the bound is then in the signature, and the compiler checks it at every
# call.  Any other call is a finding, the iterator-pair form included.  A
# type constraint has no clang-query matcher, hence the tool.
tool bounded-fold
